From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: learn the swap_pace floor from unpaced
 swaps only

With swap_pace on, a J604 panel swap that is held starts well before the
grid tick it aims at, so its start-to-completion time overstates the
firmware's floor. The window minimum then rose over a window of held
swaps, a too long lead skipped the wait while the tick between two
refreshes was still reachable, and frames landed there in bursts: on the
J604, 18 of 297 frames of a 60 fps video, 12 of them within one window.

Learn the floor from unpaced swaps only and keep the estimate while
swap_pace is on. Without an estimate use 1.75 ms, the shortest swap to
completion time measured on the J604 (1.71 to 1.82 ms in three runs).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 5b8d116e5a..8fc8cdf1fc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1751,6 +1751,14 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	if (!start || done <= start)
 		return;
 	WRITE_ONCE(r->int_start_cnt, 0);
+	/*
+	 * A paced swap starts on purpose well before the tick it aims at, so
+	 * its start-to-completion time overstates the floor, and a window of
+	 * them would raise the estimate by up to a tick each time. Learn from
+	 * unpaced swaps only; the estimate stands while swap_pace is on.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(swap_pace))
+		return;
 	lat = done - start;
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
 		r->int_lat_win = lat;
@@ -2660,7 +2668,7 @@ static unsigned long dcp_m4_swap_pace_us(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	if (lead_us)
 		lead = div_u64(freq * lead_us, USEC_PER_SEC);
 	else
-		lead = READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq, 500);
+		lead = READ_ONCE(r->int_lat_min) ?: div_u64(freq * 7, 4000);
 	/* The first grid tick base + k * half (k even) at least lead + margin ahead. */
 	k = div64_u64(now + lead + margin - base + half - 1, half);
 	k += k & 1;
